{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Elohim remembered Noah.</b> It would have been fitting for Scripture to say 'Noah and his sons,' for we find that the divine speech addressed them as well, as it is written, 'And Elohim said to Noah and to his sons.' It is possible to say that the particle את comes to include his sons, who were of his issue, just as the Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted 'את יעקב' — these are those who come from the issue of Jacob. And since Scripture explained this remembrance by way of 'issue' and alluded to the sons, the women too were included. And the fact that He mentioned the beast and the animal together with him is to indicate that all are equal in general providence; and by the same token the remembrance extended to all the fowl, even though He did not mention them, for all living creatures are included in the remembrance. Or perhaps the reason He mentioned specifically 'בהמה וחיה' and did not mention the fowl is that the beast and the animal were created together with man on the sixth day, as it is written, 'And Elohim made every beast of the earth after its kind, and the cattle after their kind' — and this is what is meant by 'אשר אתו' — that they are with him in the ark. And 'אשר אתו' may also include those that were created on the same day with him."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:11:04.766762913Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}